			"local_notes": "Lore: The human-portable bolt pistol, most commonly the Godwyn-De'az pattern firing a lighter mass-reactive round than the Astartes-scale weapons, is issued to Inquisitorial acolytes, commissars, veteran officers and other elite humans rather than to rank-and-file Guardsmen, who are more usually equipped with an autopistol or laspistol if they carry a sidearm at all. Dark Heresy and Rogue Trader both depict it as a prized weapon whose recoil is punishing for an unaugmented shooter (this project rates it LC1).\n\nDesign: A human-scale bolt weapon, not a scaled-down Astartes one: it fires a smaller-calibre .60-ish round with a lighter mass-reactive charge sized for a hand a Guardsman or acolyte can actually close around, so it drops the Astartes-scale pi++ wounding multiplier to pi and shrinks the frag follow-up from the boltgun anchor's 2d cr ex down to 1d-1 cr ex - a genuinely smaller warhead, not the same shell in a shorter barrel. Dice and armour divisor stay one die down from the Godwyn boltgun anchor (5dx2(2), divisor (2) unchanged) since the rocket motor still ignites clear of the muzzle and does the real accelerating; only the wounding mechanism and burst yield shrink. Exact dice distribution: 5dx2(2) averages 35 and penetrates carapace (DR 70, effective DR 35) on 50.0% of hits, Sororitas power armour (DR 85, effective DR 42.5) on 15.2%, and Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective DR 50) on just 1.6% - a coin-flip against carapace, a real but unreliable threat to Sororitas plate, and essentially no threat to a Space Marine, exactly the gap a smaller human-portable round should leave against the Astartes-scale anchor. Special ammunition (Kraken, Hellfire, etc.) is not repeated here; see the Boltgun, Godwyn Pattern entry for the loads, which a GM may allow in this pistol's lighter round with the same pi and follow-up reductions. Handling: 5 lb loaded, in line with Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader's roughly 2.5 kg figure for a human-portable bolt pistol. Min ST 10† (√(10×5)≈7, bumped up three for the punishing recoil of a mass-reactive round fired from a pistol frame - unusually high for a service pistol, compare a normal GURPS pistol's ST 8-9) reflects the \"hard for unaugmented humans to handle\" property the fiction keeps returning to; the † lets it be fired two-handed at the listed ST, one-handed by anyone under ST 10 at the standard penalty for shooting under minimum ST. RoF 3 is the standard semi-automatic rate every boltgun in this file uses (per framework.md, a bolt weapon is not a true rapid-fire autoloader). Shots 8(3): an 8-round box magazine, short compared with a rifle's, and a quick 3-second reload. Bulk -2 and Rcl 3 are ordinary pistol figures, the latter elevated slightly above a stub pistol's for the bolt's initial kick.",
